# GitHub security triage on push (Marfa/Artalk)

Before **every `git push`** to `origin` for this repo, check and handle open items on:

| Surface | URL |
|---|---|
| Pull requests | https://github.com/Marfa/Artalk/pulls |
| Malware | https://github.com/Marfa/Artalk/security/malware |
| Dependabot | https://github.com/Marfa/Artalk/security/dependabot |
| Code scanning | https://github.com/Marfa/Artalk/security/code-scanning |
| Secret scanning | https://github.com/Marfa/Artalk/security/secret-scanning |

Prefer `gh` over scraping HTML.

## Checklist (run, then act)

```bash
gh pr list --repo Marfa/Artalk --state open
gh api repos/Marfa/Artalk/dependabot/alerts --paginate --jq '[.[] | select(.state=="open")]'
gh api repos/Marfa/Artalk/code-scanning/alerts?state=open
gh api repos/Marfa/Artalk/secret-scanning/alerts?state=open
```

Malware: open the malware security URL (or matching API if available). Treat HTTP 404 / empty as “nothing open or feature not enabled” — say so in the response, do not invent alerts.

If code/secret scanning returns 404, the feature is off or inaccessible — report that once; do not block the push solely for that.

## How to handle

### Dependabot PRs (`pulls`)

- CI green + mergeable patch/security bump → merge (`gh pr merge --merge` or `--squash` matching repo default).
- Conflicts or red CI → rebase/fix locally, push branch, recheck, then merge.
- Superseded by a broader local bump → close with a short comment pointing at the fixing commit.

### Dependabot alerts

- Patched version exists → bump direct dep and/or add `pnpm.overrides` for transitive packages, refresh `pnpm-lock.yaml`, commit.
- Advisory **withdrawn** or clearly inaccurate (no fixed version, GHSA withdrawn) → dismiss via API with `inaccurate` (or `not_used` when the package is not reachable at runtime for this app).
- Do not dismiss high/critical reachable vulns as `tolerable_risk` without stating residual risk to the user.

### Code scanning

- True positive in our code → fix in the same push when possible.
- False positive / wontfix → dismiss with reason in GitHub; note in the response.

### Secret scanning

- Real secret → rotate immediately, remove from git history if needed, never “fix” by only deleting the line without rotation.
- False positive → mark as false positive in GitHub.

### Malware

- Open malware findings → quarantine/remove the offending dependency or file; do not push until cleared or explicitly waived by the user with residual risk named.

## Response before push

In chat, briefly report: open counts per surface, what was fixed/merged/dismissed, and anything left open with why.

## Invariants

- Never paste real secrets from alerts into chat or commits.
- Prefer env/`ATK_*` over committing credentials.
- Do not rewrite `exports/` in place while remediating.
- This is a fork of ArtalkJS/Artalk — do not add Marfa donation/Cursor README blocks here.
